Endesa and Barcelona with electric car
The electricity company Endesa, together with the Barcelona City Council, have created the 'LIVE Office'.
It is a project to develop and promote the electric vehicle in the Catalan capital.
The 'LIVE Office' (Logistics for the Implementation of the Electric Vehicle) will define and coordinate the roadmap for the implementation of the electric car in the city and will achieve agreements around mobility, managing, coordinating, presenting grants, etc.
On the other hand it will develop the MOVELE project, promote the electric car, collect the opinion and work of the sectors involved.
In short, it is intended to promote what will be the transport of the future.
3 'electric cities'
But Barcelona is not the only city that will be involved in the implementation of the electric car in Spain.
Madrid and Seville joined the project.
They are the three cities chosen by the Government, within the MOVELE Plan, to promote the implementation of the electric vehicle.
The electricity company Endesa has already signed a framework agreement with the Generalitat of Catalonia.
This aims to promote research and technological development activities in the Autonomous Community of Catalonia.
Among these would be energy-related activities and in particular energy efficiency.
It is not the only initiative in which Endesa participates in terms of the promotion of the electric vehicle.
The company participates in standardization groups at European level and has assets a number of complementary projects such as G4V, ELVIRE or CENIT VERDE.
Zapatero sees 'a horizon of tranquility' for the engine sector
The president of the Government, José Luis Rodríguez Zapatero, glimpses "a horizon of tranquility" for the Spanish automotive industry, which, he recalled, is the main exporting sector in the country.
In the presentation of the Economic Report of the President of the Government for 2009, Zapatero reviewed the measures that the Executive has put in place throughout the year to support the automotive sector.
"Without the Automotive Competitiveness Plan, today we would have a panorama of abandonment, the closure of some of our major productive plants," said the president of the government.
"Thanks to this plan and at the disposal of the brands to follow in Spain, in a very competitive sector, we can have a horizon of tranquility for the future of this industry, which is our main exporting sector," he added.
In this sense, he recalled that the Competitiveness Plan, included in the Comprehensive Automotive Plan (PIA), allocated 800 million to projects of 19 manufacturers and 137 auxiliary companies, which mobilized an investment of more than 3,000 million euros.
The head of the Executive explained that this investment was committed both for the development of new models and to modernize existing products and processes.
Zapatero also emphasized government demand support measures, referring to Plan 2000E, implemented in collaboration with the autonomous communities and automotive brands.
According to the president, this plan has allowed to reduce by 6% the average emissions of new vehicles marketed in the Spanish market and has led to a "strong increase" of registrations, which grew "40 percent" in November.
20,000 square meters of classic vehicles
There will be held in Madrid the first edition of the International Exhibition of the Classic Vehicle, a meeting space for professionals and amateurs from the engine.
This initiative will take place from 5 to 7 February 2010 in the Glass Pavilion of the Casa de Campo in Madrid.
It is an exhibition area of 20,000 square meters in which there will be more than 200 national and international exhibitors.
Not only can you find motorcycles and classic cars, but ClassicAuto Madrid will find items of all kinds related to the world of the engine.
Thus, among the exhibitors of the pavilion, you can find accessories, spare parts, components, textile accessories, accessories, publications, miniatures, etc.
Hundreds of articles related to the world of the classical engine that will delighten collectors and curious.
Among the participating companies you will find, among others, Mos Classics and Good Old Times, car sales; Juan Lumbreras, restoration; Coupe-Francisco Pueche sale and restoration of cars; or Classical Garage, Mercedes Benz specialist.
Skill tests on the outside
In addition, the commercial activity of this Salon will be completed with parallel activities: celebrations, sports exhibitions, skill tests, presentations and competitions.
Skill tests will also be carried out with classic cars and motorcycles on a circuit enabled outside the fairgrounds.
Mazda3 i-Stop: sustainable sportsmanship
Mazda wants to show that sportsmanship is not at odds with respect for the environment.
For this reason, it has just added to the Mazda3 the engine stop and starter system -christened as i-Stop-, a device that at least for the moment is only available with the 2.0 gasoline engine with 150 horsepower.
This second generation of the Mazda3 stands out for the good score achieved throughout its whole.
The finishes, vehicle finish, habitability, behavior, mechanics, i-Stop system...
All of these aspects are outstanding in the new Mazda3.
Starting from the driving position, we found that the front seats have excellent ergonomics and support.
Likewise, the touch of the steering wheel is exquisite.
Continuing with the set formed by the frame of instruments and the console we see how Mazda has continued the Japanese trend of creating a futuristic interior design, with a lot of buttons and knobs and striking colors in red and blue.
This style reminds us, in part, the one that also presents the Honda Civic.
Therefore, we can say that both the Mazda3 and the Civic, both Japanese, contrast with the sobriety of German products, and more specifically the Volkswagen Golf, which everyone wants to beat.
Continuing with the passenger compartment, this Japanese compact has more than enough habitability for four adults to travel with a high level of comfort.
To all this is added a large trunk with regular shapes.
The engine’s automatic stop and start system, at least for the moment, is only available with the two-litre, 150-horse-powered petrol engine with the six-speed manual transmission.
This engine is a real delight. It stands out for its finesse, for its reduced rumour, for the benefits and for achieving contained consumptions.
And it is that although the most demanded Mazda3 will be the diesel versions, those who do not perform a high number of kilometers a year should not dismiss this i-Stop with a gasoline engine, both for its high running comfort and for its contained consumption.
Regarding the level of equipment, the version chosen for the test is the so-called Sportive, i.e. the one that incorporates a greater number of serial elements.
Of the standard equipment stands out especially the lane change assistant (RVM) that eliminates dead angle, traction and stability controls, speed control, photosensitive interior mirror, on-board computer on a large screen, parking sensors, independent air conditioner, rain and light sensor, bluetooth and bluetooth audio and 17-inch alloy wheels.
In addition, as if it were not enough, this version had the Premium Pack, which adds for 1,500 euros: bixenon adaptive headlights and BOSE sound system with disc charger, among other elements.
Conclusion
The Mazda3 2.0 i-Stop is one of the best compacts in the category.
It stands out especially for the quality of the materials used, for their behavior and for the high level of equipment.
In addition, those who do not make many kilometers a year will be able to opt for this i-Stop version, associated only with the 150-horsepower 2.0 gasoline engine.
The only drawback of this model is its high price, which stands between 21,770 euros of the Luxury finish and the 23,270 euros of the proven version -Sportive-.
In exchange for this high figure, the Mazda3 will offer us every day large doses of satisfaction.
