Fine of 63 million to France Télécom for curbing competition
The competition regulator in France has imposed a fine of 63 million euros on France Télécom for anti-competitive conduct in the Caribbean regions belonging to the country.
According to this institution, the operator limited the competition in fixed and mobile telephony with the signing of exclusive agreements, price plans and consumer loyalty programs outside the regulation.
With this sanction, the old French monopoly and still state company accumulates more than 560 million euros in fines since 1994 for putting obstacles to its competitors.
The sentence imposed yesterday, in fact, has been increased because the competent authority considers that France Télécom has committed similar infringements in the past and that, therefore, it is a repeat offender.
App store
On the other hand, the mobile subsidiary of the French company has followed the wake of other operators and has opened an online application store, with the aim of increasing revenue that does not come from voice transmission.
In principle, the Orange app store will be active in France and the United Kingdom.
We will have to wait until 2010 to reach other countries, such as Spain.
Playing the Champions League has reported 476.4 million to Madrid and Barça since its origin
The Champions League has become a source of income for clubs since it was born in 1992.
So mutically, that Real Madrid and Barcelona have entered 476.4 million since then, which makes them the third and fifth clubs that have earned the most money in the competition.
The leader of the list is Manchester United.
The leader of the list is Manchester United.
Earning the UEFA Champions League not only provides glory. It is also one of the main sources of revenue of the big clubs.
So much so, that the competition has distributed 5,362.5 million euros to the 105 teams (12 of them Spanish) that have participated in the event since the tournament was created in the 1992/1993 season, according to UEFA data.
Real Madrid and F. C. Barcelona have gone well on this cast.
The white club has been the third of the continent that has pocketed the most to participate, and the only one, along with AC Milan, who has won the trophy three times.
The Catalan, the reigning champion and the last winner of the extinct European Cup in 1992, is the fifth of qualifying.
The list is led by Manchester United and Bayern Munich, the two teams that, in addition, more money billed for participating in the last Champions League.
And that, despite losing both against Barça.
On the other hand, Spain is only the third country that has achieved more money through the Champions League, despite having achieved more titles than any other (five, for the four of Italy, the three of England and the two of Germany).
Distribution
This apparent paradox is explained by UEFA’s complicated money-sharing procedure.
For this year, Michel Platini’s presiding body plans to enter 1.090 million for the Champions League.
From this money UEFA will dedicate 413.1 million for fixed payments: each of the 20 clubs that participated in the previous qualifying round (including Atlético de Madrid) received 2.1 million.
In addition, those who managed to participate received 3.8 million just for being there, in addition to another 550,000 euros for each match they play.
There are also bonuses for winning (800,000 euros) and for scoring (400,000 for each team). The eighth finalists will receive three million each; the eight quarter-finalists, 3.3 million.
The last four will pocket 4 million each.
The champion will win 9 million, compared to 5.2 million from the finalist.
Thus, in terms of fixed payments, a club will enter at least 7.1 million, and a maximum of 31.2 million.
Barça, on the other hand, pocketed 2.5 million for winning the European Super Cup in August.
But it is also that there are variable payments, to which 337.8 million are allocated.
This money is distributed according to the proportional value of each television market.
Spaniard is one of the main ones, and has four assigned places.
The champion of the previous year stays with 40% of the money allocated, 30% for the second, 20% for the third and 10% for the fourth.
The other party will be paid according to the number of matches played in this year’s edition.
Nueva Rumasa offers 61 million euros for 29.9% of Sos
The Nueva Rumasa group yesterday outlined the details of the offer of purchase of shares with which it seeks to acquire a cap of between 25% and 29.9% of the capital of Sos.
A percentage that does not oblige you to launch an offer of public acquisition (opa) for all of the securities.
