CNMV authorizes Paternina exclusion opa filed by Inversora Mer
The National Securities Market Commission (CNMV) yesterday authorized the opt-out filed by Investora Mer on Federico Paternina on October 9.
The supervising body has explained that it authorizes this operation on the understanding that its terms comply with the current rules and consider "sufficient" the content of the explanatory brochure presented after the modifications made on December 2.
The CNMV has specified that the offer is aimed at the acquisition of 550.008 shares of Federico Paternina at a price of 7.65 euros per share, which represents 8.95% of its share capital, which is composed of 6,142,786 shares admitted to trading on the Madrid and Bilbao Stock Exchanges.
Likewise, it has explained that 5,592,778 million shares have been immobilized, which cannot be transmitted in any way until the end of the offer, of which it has specified that the price has been fixed by Federico Paternina, in accordance with the provisions of current regulations.
New tools to harvest cars
In these days of temps and accidents, they don’t just win the car workshops.
Every day thousands of cars that have suffered a loss are towed to a workshop, where an expert must evaluate the damage suffered and what will be the repair cost.
No loss is the same, and the calculation of parts costs and labor time can be long and complicated.
Calculating manually the cost of a repair of between 20,000 and 30,000 euros, including parts and labor, can take two or three hours.
On the other hand, with the support of the most recent computer tools it would be a matter of minutes
For this reason, almost 100% of experts use this type of systems.
Providers of services and solutions for claims and maintenance are dedicated to collecting the information provided to them by manufacturers, and then prepare it and offer it to their customers in the form of a useful tool.
In Spain, Audatex, of the American group Solera, is the leading firm; 80% of the valuations are made with its products.
The other firms that compete in the field of appraisal and information-making tools on the sector are GtMotive and Eurotax.
The work with the data provided by manufacturers is far from simple.
According to Eduardo Velázquez, commercial director of Audatex, in Spain they work with 63 manufacturers and importers, and each of them supplies them with the information in different formats.
In addition, the amount of data to be processed continues to increase, to the point that in the last five years more versions, variants and motorizations have been released than in the previous fifteen.
As soon as a new car hits the market, these companies get to work.
It is a very arduous task, because you have to catalog each of the thousands of parts of the vehicle and introduce its price.
In addition, from each model a "smart" graphic image is made where you can "puncture" different parts of tourism.
If it’s a massive selling model, the job may be ready in a week if the process goes very fast.
If it is a minority car, it can take three or four months. Currently, Audatex has complete information on 99.2% of the cars that are marketed in Spain.
Among the most exclusive models they have information about Porsche, but not Ferrari or Lamborghini, for example.
As for the mobile park that circulates, they exceed 99%.
To carry out the work of documentation and the elaboration of the databases, Audatex has eight centers scattered around the world (Spain, France, Germany, USA, Brazil, Mexico, China and Japan), and each of them is specialized in specific brands.
The national headquarters are in Alcobendas (Madrid).
There, more than one hundred technicians (usually mechanical experts) work simultaneously with three computer screens.
Audatex invests 90 million euros per year in developing these databases.
2.5 million data is included each month, and customers receive updates every two days.
The elaboration of this enormous flow of information allows these companies to give them different uses and offer various products.
The most frequent use focuses on repair and maintenance, but according to which countries there are also tools for the management of scrapping parts or to calculate the venal or residual value of a car.
The only company that has a guide that informs about the value of those used in Spain is Eurotax.
Audatex doesn’t offer it in our country, but in the United States.
In view of the products offered by Audatex it is easy to get an idea of the type of support they can lend to professionals in the sector.
This company offers ten different tools, being the star product AudaPlus, the standard singer valuation solution, intended for experts.
Includes cars, motorcycles and light or heavy commercial vehicles.
In addition to the cost of the parts, it includes the repair times estimated by the manufacturer or paint scales.
This tool is paid according to usage, for each valuation.
The highest cost is 5.75 euros, for customers who use it little, a maximum of ten times a month.
Then each insurance company, which performs thousands of expertise, negotiates its price with Audatex.
Other products, such as AudaVIN, allow the total identification of a vehicle and the equipment with which it left the assembly line only with its frame number.
AudaGlass concentrates on the moons of vehicles, and AudaSubastas is a service open to the professional sector on the Internet that allows you to bid for vehicles declared total sinister.
Its statistics service is very useful to identify trends, perform geodemographic analyses or know deviations by brands or models.
You can study, for example, how many models of a certain brand have passed through the workshop due to breakdowns or how many have suffered serious accidents in a certain period.
Gt Motive is the only Spanish company dedicated to the development of such tools.
Commercialize, among others, Gt Estimate, which is also intended for experts and also provides digital images, access to parts or prices and official times of the manufacturer.
Gt Motive is an Einsa group company founded in 1971 as a provider of services and solutions for damage, breakdowns or car maintenance
Gt Appraisals Guide is its historical reference product in the market.
They work with 24,000 users in workshops, 3,100 experts and 53 insurance companies.
Their turnover has grown at a rate of 20% annually in the last three years, and in 2008 they billed 10.8 million euros.
At the beginning of last year they began their process of internationalization, with the installation of an office in Paris.
Audatex was born in Germany in 1966 and in 1979 was established in Spain.
According to sources of the company, 62% of its business is generated in Europe and the rest of the world, and the remaining 38%, in North and South America. They work with 900 insurance companies and 33,000 workshops, 3,000 of them in Spain.
The global turnover of the Solera group (Audatex, Sidexa, Informex ABZ, Hollander and IMS) will reach 557 million dollars, 3.3% more than in 2008.
In our country the company will enter 19.1 million euros, 7.2% more than the previous year.
In 2005, the Solera group was worth one billion dollars on the Stock Exchange, and now its shares are listed for a total value of 2.4 billion dollars.
Since 2007 it is listed on the New York Stock Exchange and is included in the Standard & Poor's benchmark index.
Internet Auction of Rugged Cars
Last October, the Solera group bought Autoonline, an internet platform for the sale of cars such as motorcycles or special vehicles.
The operation resulted in an outlay of 59.5 million euros for 85% of the capital of the company, which could be extended next year to the remaining 15%.
The objective of the acquisition was to offer more value-added services to its customers, with the possibility of accessing an immense international market.
This valuation and sales service is aimed exclusively at professionals in the sector, such as insurance companies, experts, renting companies, workshops, scrapyards and professional vendors who must register before starting operations.
This platform was created in 1996 in Germany and manages more than 650,000 operations across Europe, 500,000 of them in Germany.
Among its main markets are Spain, Greece, Poland and Turkey.
The website currently has more than 1,500 registered sellers and 4,000 experts.
3,000 ads are managed daily and about 100 new announcements are included in the Spanish market every day.
Under Spanish law, a car whose rack number has been discharged cannot recirculate, but certain undamaged parts can be used as a replacement.
Cars with historical value can be discharged even if they have been discharged after some burdensome efforts.
Four-Step Workshop Quote
With the Auda-Workshop tool, Audatex guarantees that the user obtains a budget in only four steps: identify the vehicle, look for the replacement, create budget and generate budget.
Ease-of-use is an essential condition for these systems, especially to convince older professionals, who to a greater or lesser extent are usually more reluctant to use new management techniques.
The database includes 1,034 vehicles, which are 666 passenger cars, 109 SUVs, 137 motorcycles, 78 vans and 44 trucks.
Naturally, to use it you need a computer with an internet connection.
Once the model to be repaired has been identified using its frame number, an actual graphic image of the model in question appears, and then the necessary replacement is selected.
The user can include variables such as labor price, surcharges or discounts, and then can print the budget to deliver to the customer.
AudaTaller is not a valuation tool like AudaPlus, but rather a catalog of references.
The main difference between the two systems is that the workshop-oriented one does not include estimated labor times.
The cost of using this tool for the workshop is 350 euros per year, which the client can finance.
Audatex is currently working to make these images three-dimensional.
This is an innovation that the mechanics see with very good eyes, since it will allow, for example, to select a door and turn it around to see the inner face.
